# /etc/immich-integrity-exceptions
#
# Asset UUIDs whose file on disk disagrees with Immich's recorded checksum,
# investigated and found NOT to be disk corruption. One UUID per line.
# verify_immich_source_integrity.sh skips these but still reports the count.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-08-28/29: six assets, and every one is a corrupted RECORD, not a
# corrupted file. For each: WBU and FleetNAS hold identical bytes, the file is
# structurally valid, and its size matches Immich's own EXIF record exactly.
# Only the stored checksum disagrees -- and it disagrees with both copies
# rather than matching either.
#
# Immich hashes a file once, in memory, at ingest. All six were ingested on
# 2026-06-23, the day 45,482 assets (65% of the library) were imported in a
# single session, inside the window when this machine ran four mismatched
# DIMMs. Six bad records in 45,482 is roughly 1 in 7,580 -- what marginal
# memory does over a long sustained import.
#
# Note the correlation is the INGEST DATE, not file size: the six range from
# 2.4 MB to 5.4 GB. An earlier reading of this as a large-file effect was
# wrong.
#
# Remove an entry if Immich ever recomputes checksums and the database agrees
# with the disk again.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

45d01a4e-a5b6-46c6-84a4-2c779be21f26   # 5.4 GB mp4
9d8cb158-b14f-4477-bca2-d204ffa90773   # 2.0 GB mp4
c81cb913-6860-4bbf-b9fc-adb7727703d2   # 3.0 GB mp4
3c50864a-670d-47e7-83d9-091d24d69d90   # 2.8 MB PNG, 1242x2208
931d6b61-3fee-4185-a069-f251309f1968   # 2.4 MB JPEG
c13a243b-7df3-4ad3-9074-5948ceaa4585   # 3.0 MB JPEG
